      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i just ate a huge bowl of pasta like 120g of carbs and my sugar is already climbing. i'm trying to figure out my correction dose but im confused. my doctor said my ratio is 1 unit for every 5g of carbs but then i saw a note about doing 1 unit for every 10g too. if i take 15 units of rapid insulin for this meal will that cover the carbs and the spike? i dont want to go too low but i need to get this under control.",
