      "content": "Based strictly on the ratio you provided (1 unit for every 5g of carbs), a 120g carbohydrate intake would mathematically require 24 units of insulin (120 divided by 5 equals 24). However, insulin dosing is complex and should never be determined by calculation alone when blood sugar is already elevated. Please know that while the math aligns with your stated ratio, this dosage carries risks, and you should contact an urgent care line or a dedicated diabetes nurse line if your blood sugar does not start coming down soon.",
